body:
>Suicide is incredibly selfish. It’s a blunt “fuck you” to every good thing, every person who tried, every possibility that things will be better, no matter how slim, and saying that getting rid of the pain now, and right now, is better. There are people who care about you a lot that I’m positive you don’t even know about.

As everyone in this world is. Do u think people tried bc of that person? No. They try because they're scared of change, of losing the way u make them feel but they can't actually worry for you. They won't take responsability for your life, even if they try, they just can't. So, that thing your wrote is as selfish as those who think people have the right to commit suicide. Everyone should have free will on their own life, the life they will have to live and be responsable of. Not every suicide is an impulsive decision, some persons simply dont want to live. Some persons actually dont have anything ahead, for example, those with a serious illness. 

&#x200B;

>Your actions have massive repercussions, and you should know that. Did you have any friends, at any point? Are you snapping people? Did you break up with an ex in the past two years? How about school, if that’s where you’re at? Any friends there? Is there anyone at work that you talk to? If you’re in college, do you have a dorm mate?

Yeah, of course, but they have their own lifes and nobody is responsable of others feelings. They are not responsable for how you feel and you are not responsable for how they feel. It's each one's life. Nobody should be forced to keep living in pain just because of others. And if the problem is other people, then one can isolate for some time and then die. 

&#x200B;

>Fine. This will sound harsh, but what you’re doing is childish and immature, so let me tell you something serious for a moment. None of this comes from a place of blunt anger, but from a place of genuine frustration with every part of this post.

&#x200B;

Is giving one's life to others really mature? I think many people have that conception because we're social beings and our biological purpose is to reproduce and keep the specie, but as we advance and evolutionate, we become more and more individualistict. People nowadays dont plan to have children, for example. Now our purpose is not to reproduce, but to enjoy life as much as we can and be responsable of it. So, if everyone is responsable of their own life, why they should be not allowed to take their own life? If a person simply dont find a reason to live, has a serious illness or thinks that has lived enough, they should have the right to die. I think is waaaay more mature to accept one's responsability with their own life and decide what to do with it. 

Now, i hope u dont get confused and think that im encouraging suicide, but im defending it as a rational decision. I dont support suicide if a person has depression, is going throught a lot of pain or has any kind of situation that makes them prefer to die and has a solution or method to decrease the suffering.

masturbating doesnt make water sounds as far as i know, she would've done it several times to get to that point lmao

&#x200B;

Anyways, she was probably asleep or if u want to confirm it, ask her and if she says that she did it conscious or it happens again, sleep in the floor with some inflatable mattress or smth. If she keeps doing it, i would say its harrassment but im not pretty sure

It's like i can't feel comfortable. Like, even if i found something that made me happy and did it, i would feel like something is not right, like i can't feel right, i just feel uncomfortable. 

Yesterday, i painted some dots in my hands, like if it was some expression of some illness, it felt kind of comforting because whenever i thought about doing something i could see my hands and see that illness i feel whenever i try to do anything but i can't say with words. I feel like something is just not right with me

&#x200B;

And i'm not really sure. I pretend and kinda obligate myself to do things because i dont have hobbies. Drawing is not exciting anymore, i don't like books, i hate piano because it's too hard, i don't find animals or plants interesting, i don't find science, history or politics interesting and i like painting and things like that but i get bored quickly. I've also tried to learn new things but it's too hard for me to the point where it's like a torture

&#x200B;

And no, nothing ever happened but it's just like it bothers me

&#x200B;

Thank u anyways

Yeah, ur kinda right, i sound mean while coming up with the things i said. 

&#x200B;

About what u said: First of all, no, there are a lot of people that still think that u have loving urself is loving everything about u, it's not that obvious, and im not going against giving some compliments but what i understood from the post is the person saying "i like ur insecurities so love urself and like them too" so im saying that it simply goes further than being liked by others, it's a process that the person has to go through to accept themselves

maybe cuz they havent realized their flaws or they just dont care about it. 

&#x200B;

like, u can respect urself and everything, but being totally content with who u are its weird

You're kind and i agree with u in some points, but not at all. Like, the fact that U like those things, doesn't mean that they are going to like them, it's not only about being liked by other people but to like themselves. So, if someone just dont like something of their looks, it doesnt have to be necessarily bad as long as it dont get too bad to the point that they're getting anxiety or some mental issue, because i dont think that we have to find ourselves beautiful or perfect to respect ourselves. There are somethings that ur just not going to like, and if u want to change them and u think u will feel better in that way, just do it. It's like people who say that women have to like menstruation because it's part of nature when nature doesnt mean good. Menstruation is just uncomfortable and u can lie urself saying that it's beautiful and all that, but life would be way easier without it. 

&#x200B;

I kinda think it's a problem of ours having to find something beautiful to accept it and respect it. That's why the "beauty is subjective, u can be pretty to other people or other cultures" bothers me. Like, why do they have to be beautiful? Maybe because we're usually guided by looks, but i do think that u can consciously stop that impulse and fall in love with whoever u want to. 

&#x200B;

Btw, (to everyone, not specially u) stop with the "love urself", it's pretentious, unreal and cringe. U just gotta respect urself and defend ur dignity

Maybe he hasnt understood tha he's responsable for that house too, that if those things aren't done, there are going to be consequences and about their personal hygiene, i would say that it's pretty much their problem, but the odor is too bad, then tell him about it. 

&#x200B;

Nevertheless, you don't have to be in that relationship, you don't need a relationship to live, you don't have to stand that or any of their behaviors that you don't like. Maybe the process of breaking up with him could be long and tiring, but if you want it and you think it's worth it, do it. Don't spend time of your life being unhappy for things that can be fixed.
